OL,3,GNorth West
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FCool and cloudy, though with
OL,6,Fthe occasional brighter spell. Dry for
OL,7,Fmost, though there is a risk of
OL,8,Fisolated drizzly showers, mainly over
OL,9,Fnorthern hills. A gentle breeze, and
OL,10,Ftemperatures near average for the time
OL,11,Fof year.
OL,12,
OL,13,CTonight:FA cloudy, chilly night but
OL,14,Fremaining dry for most. Winds will
OL,15,Fease to a light breeze by the evening.
OL,16,FTemperatures close to average for the
OL,17,Ftime of year.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
FL,166,160,301,260,100,100
PN,16502
SC,0002
CT,20,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F165A1793850457
OL,1,Wj5hw1~{4k7juhw1{$             G2/2
OL,2,W+.-'"-$/*%*%*%/"-$/*%Q,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNorth West
OL,4,
OL,5,CFriday:FAnother cloudy day, with only
OL,6,Ffew brighter breaks. Drier than
OL,7,FThursday, with drizzly showers
OL,8,Fconfined to hills. A light, cool
OL,9,Fbreeze, and temperatures close to the
OL,10,Fseasonal average.
OL,11,
OL,12,COutlook for Saturday to Monday:FCool
OL,13,Fand cloudy conditions persisting
OL,14,Fthrough Saturday, with the odd shower.
OL,15,FBecoming increasingly clear through
OL,16,FSunday and Monday with pleasant
OL,17,Fautumnal sunshine, and colder nights
OL,18,Fbringing frost and fog.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
FL,166,160,301,260,100,100
